  "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{A}={{a}_{2},{a}_{5},{a}_{7},{a}_{8}}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{B}={{a}_{2},{a}_{4},{a}_{6},{a}_{8}},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B}?$",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{B} \\\\  & ={{a}_{2},{a}_{5},{a}_{7},{a}_{8}}\\cap {{a}_{2},{a}_{4},{a}_{6},{a}_{8}} \\\\  & ={{a}_{2},{a}_{8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
